 "new_string": "Task ID also has diagonal-marker periodic-texture variants; classify geometry first. Stripe demos in this instance had varied cycles not trivially source-order, first-occurrence unique colors, or sorted colors: `[2,8,5]`, `[9,9,1,7,6,4]`, `[8,4,7,9,1]`, `[3,4,7,7,1,4]`, `[6,5]`. Do not infer a universal permutation law from `[5,3,7]`.\n\n## Fresh accepted diagonal-strand variant (2026-11)\nTest 16x16: sparse parallel diagonals; color 6 on `r-c=-4..-1`, color 9 on `r-c=-2..1`, color 8 on `r-c=-2..-1`, color 5 on `r-c=9` (0-based; equivalently input rows have the listed descending/ascending diagonal tracks). Output accepted as a full 16x16 texture depending only on `(r+c) mod 4`, with sequence `[6,9,8,5]`: `out[r][c] = [6,9,8,5][(r+c)%4]`. Thus row0 is `[6,9,8,5]` repeated; each subsequent row shifts phase left by one, repeating every four rows.\n\nEvidence from demos in that run: a 26x26 set of strands produced a period-6 texture with top row `[2,7,3,5,1,3]` repeated; another 22x22 diagonal case produced period 4 with `[9,5,7,8]` repeated; a 10x10 multi-strand case produced period 6 `[8,6,5,3,5,9,1,4]` actually period 8; a 12x12 case produced period 5 `[7,9,7,1,2]`. These show period and palette vary. Crucially, accepted test output sequence was directly [6,9,8,5] from its observed stripe colors, indexed by anti-diagonal sum modulo 4. Do not use the earlier rejected guess `[2,7,3,5,1,3]`-family for this test. Geometry: parallel tracks with slope -1 encode an anti-diagonal periodic texture; determine period from stripe/track structure and infer phase/order from marker colors and anchors. Recheck against fresh demos as task variants differ."
